  "solution": {
    "text": "All statements are correct <br/><math><msub><mrow><mtext>B</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo></math> acidic , <math><msub><mrow><mtext>B</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> is an anhydride of Orthoboric Acid. <br/><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> are amphoteric, amphoteric oxides can react with acids as well as bases. <br/>oxides of ln and Tl are basic. <br/>As we move down the group basicity of oxides increases due to increase in metallic character of elements",
